    {
      "id": "ML-C50-day-after",
      "sequence": 1400,
      "title": "മറ്റന്നാൾ (maṟṟannāḷ) — the day after tomorrow",
      "headword": "മറ്റന്നാൾ",
      "romanization": "maṟṟannāḷ",
      "gloss": "the day after tomorrow",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:1af3e03a08216b59",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did ippōḷ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: മറ്റന്നാൾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മറ്റന്നാൾ (maṟṟannāḷ) — \"the day after tomorrow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three pieces, and the last of them this book has already taught: നാൾ, the native day-word. Before it sits മറ്റ് (maṟṟŭ), 'other', and a middle piece pointing at a particular day. Put together: the other day along."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Malayalam does not stop there. There is a word for the day after that one as well, and speakers use it without ceremony, where an English speaker would give up and name a date."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kannada builds its own with the same idea and different parts, ನಾಡಿದ್ದು (nāḍiddu), and its day-word is the cousin of ours."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: now, and the day after tomorrow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "maṟṟannāḷ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *maṟṟannāḷ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ippōḷ, then maṟṟannāḷ, the nearest time and a far one",
              "spoken": true,
