    {
      "id": "ML-C50-parayuka",
      "sequence": 1405,
      "title": "പറയുക (paṟayuka) — the verb behind the goodbye",
      "headword": "പറയുക",
      "romanization": "paṟayuka",
      "gloss": "to say, to tell — the verb this chapter's farewell is built on, and the one the book has used without naming",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:4e3425cd8b14f176",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ñān cintikkunnu. One word for the present, whoever is doing it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Today's verb runs on the same machine, and you have met it before without being told what it was."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പറയുക — paṟayuka — to say, to tell."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഞാൻ പറയുന്നു. — ñān paṟayunnu — \"I say.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past പറഞ്ഞു (paṟaññu), future paṟayuṁ. And like cintikkunnu, പറയുന്നു is the whole present tense — one word for ñān, nī and avar alike."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have met this verb once already without being told. The politeness chapter printed paṟayū, \"please tell me\" — the respectful request form, stem plus -ൂ. The stem under it is today's word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It arrives here because the rest of this chapter needs it: Malayalam does not have a single word for to say goodbye. It names the thing being given — a journey, a leave — and hangs this verb off it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പറ (paṟa) is the stem, and the റ in it is the hard ṟ — made further back in the mouth than the ordinary r, and one of the letters this script keeps apart where English has a single shape."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where the other three verbs in this strand came from Sanskrit nouns — cintikkuka from ചിന്ത, cōdikkuka from a Sanskrit word for pushing — this one did not. പറ is a native Dravidian stem, and it is the one this language reaches for when somebody speaks, with no other job attached."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "-ഉക (-uka) is the dictionary ending you have seen on every verb in this book: aṟiyuka, cintikkuka, cōdikkuka, cērkkuka."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "paṟayuka … ñān paṟayunnu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *paṟayuka* … *ñān paṟayunnu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ñān cintikkunnu and ñān paṟayunnu one after the other",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ñān cintikkunnu* and *ñān paṟayunnu* one after the other]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "which part of those two words is the same, and what it does",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: which part of those two words is the same, and what it does]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the request form from the politeness chapter — paṟayū",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the request form from the politeness chapter — *paṟayū*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is to say? (Paṟayuka.) What is I say? (Ñān paṟayunnu.) Does that form change when somebody else is the one saying? (No — one present tense for everybody.) Which ending does it share with every other verb in this book? (-ഉക.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ML-C50-journey",
      "sequence": 1410,
      "title": "യാത്ര (yātra) — a journey",
      "headword": "യാത്ര",
      "romanization": "yātra",
      "gloss": "a journey",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
